 lopsided re-election contest. Incumbent Josh Shapiro leads State Senator Stacy Garrity by roughly 20 to 25 points in every recent poll, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters like Susquehanna and National Public Affairs. A Quinnipiac poll in early October showed a 25-point margin, and averages across aggregators cluster around 21 to 23 points.\n\nAll seven expert raters classify the race as Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Shapiro's chances at 97 to 98 percent. The two candidates met in an October debate that covered immigration, the economy, and Shapiro's national ambitions, but there is no sign it shifted the race. Garrity has struggled to gain traction against a well-funded, popular incumbent in a state where Shapiro won decisively in 2022.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9934, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 21.0}, {"